# Local dev env for the Expo app. Separate from the repo root's .env
# (which apps/web/apps/api load via dotenv-cli) because Metro reads
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* vars natively from an .env file at THIS app's own root —
# there's no dotenv-cli wrapper step here, and mobile only ever needs one
# variable (a single client-side app talking to the API over HTTP, unlike
# web's server-vs-browser API_URL/NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL split).
#
#   cp .env.development.example .env
#
# Which host reaches your locally-running API (apps/api's `pnpm dev`,
# port 4000) depends on where the app is running:
#
#   - iOS Simulator: `localhost` works as-is — the Simulator shares the
#     Mac's own network stack.
#   - Physical device (Expo Go or a dev build) on the same WiFi: replace
#     with your machine's LAN IP, e.g. http://192.168.1.23:4000 — find it
#     with `ipconfig getifaddr en0` (macOS Wi-Fi) or `en1`/`en0` may vary.
#   - Android emulator: use http://10.0.2.2:4000 — a special alias the
#     emulator provides to reach the host machine, not a real IP.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000
